<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liber Paradisus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1256">1256</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liber Paradisus is a law of the commune of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a>, issued in 1256 and recorded in 1257, which freed the serfs of the city's countryside by buying their freedom from their lords. It lists the names of nearly 6,000 serfs and their owners, and the freed peasants became taxpayers of the commune. It is often cited as an early act of emancipation from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liber-paradisus.jpg" alt="Liber Paradisus" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Plessi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plessi,_Giuseppe_%E2%80%93_Liber_paradisus,_1956_%E2%80%93_BEIC_15137263.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
